  "premise_review": [
    "FiniteZeroConfiguration retains exactly n : Nat, pos : Fin n → Real and the supplied strictlyIncreasing proof for i.val < j.val. No nonempty or positive-n assumption is added; n=0 and n=1 remain allowed and the order condition is correspondingly vacuous.",
    "pairwiseRepulsionVelocity is exactly the original noncomputable finite sum, excluding j=k by an if and otherwise using 2/(X.pos k-X.pos j). No denominator lower bound, sign, continuity, ODE relation, dynamical existence or repulsion theorem is proved. The function has no k input at n=0; for an input k when n=1 only the diagonal term occurs. These are scope observations, not newly proved declarations.",
    "ArithmeticProgressionConfiguration X preserves real spacing, the strict hypothesis 0<spacing and the full pairwise real equation for every i,j : Fin X.n. It supplies positive-spacing data, not an existence proof for such data on an arbitrary configuration and not an integer progression or limiting equilibrium theorem. No basepoint/translation is fixed.",
    "finite_zero_config_ordered preserves X, implicit i/j and the strict Nat inequality h; its actual proof is exactly X.strictlyIncreasing i j h.",
    "ZeroFlowStep retains before, after, real dt and arbitrary updateLaw : Prop in the exact archive. It neither supplies a proof of updateLaw nor links that proposition to the velocity, elapsed time, positions or any Euler/ODE update equation. No field is deleted to manufacture a narrower step type.",
    "The companion modules share one explicit new variant namespace and use a fully named GRWTSK OrderedConfiguration import before the original module doc. This reuses the exact copied complete finite configuration, with no alias to an unrelated Scratch/provider type. Historical Folder import remains explicit and unresolved."
  ],
